; bfsodium DECRYPT192 : AES_192 inverse cipher on one block
;
; NOTE square brackets are brainfuck loops  so comments use braces for counts;
;
; HAND WRITTEN; block/aes128table block/aeskeyexpand192 block/invsbox256
; block/rkreverse208 block/rkconsume208 and block/aesdroundlast are INCLUDED
; and aes/addroundkey and aes/invmixcolumns are PASTED;
;
; IO  in:  key{24} block{16}
;     out: block{16}
;
; FIPS 197 section 5 point 3  the straightforward inverse cipher  with Nk of
; six and Nr of twelve;
;
; THE SCHEDULE IS MADE FORWARD AND THEN TURNED ROUND; there is no backward
; key schedule here; aes/decrypt128 has one: it keeps the last round key and
; ten temps and REGRESSES the recurrence  and that is why it needs no
; buffer; This cipher has a buffer already  because the forward cipher at
; this key size needed one  so the whole schedule is built the ordinary way
; and block/rkreverse208 turns it round once; The conveyor then runs
; unchanged  sixteen bytes off the front per round exactly as an encryption
; does  and the round keys arrive last to first because the BUFFER is
; backwards rather than because the consumer is;
;
; THE TABLE IS SWAPPED  NOT SUPPLEMENTED; the schedule needs the FORWARD S
; box for SubWord and the rounds need the INVERSE one for InvSubBytes  and
; both are read by the same walk at the same address; So the forward table is
; laid  the schedule is run  the forward table is CLEARED and the inverse
; written into the same cells; The clear is not optional: block/invsbox256 is
; a delta coded run that assumes every cell begins at nought  and written
; over a live table it would produce 256 wrong entries and sixteen plausible
; bytes;
;
; WHICH IS WHY block/aesdroundlast CONTAINS NO InvSubBytes CODE; its sixteen
; walks are character for character block/aesroundlast's  and they become
; InvSubBytes by virtue of what is resident; The forward vectors therefore
; pin the walk that the inverse ones use;
;
; THE ROUNDS ARE NOT THE FORWARD ROUNDS BACKWARDS; FIPS 197's straightforward
; inverse puts AddRoundKey BEFORE InvMixColumns  where the forward cipher
; puts it after  so the loop body here is InvShiftRows InvSubBytes
; AddRoundKey InvMixColumns and the twelfth round drops the InvMixColumns;
;
; TAPE MAP  (home @0)
;   @0x000:0x018  aes/xorword and aes/xtime workspace  inside the schedule
;   @0x019:0x030  window{24}  the key is read here  CLEARED before the rounds
;   @0x02f:0x061  aes/invmixcolumns pasted at 47  so its state is the state
;   @0x052:0x061  state{16}  the block is read here and emitted from here
;   @0x062:0x071  key{16}  one round key at a time  off the conveyor
;   @0x072:0x374  group 0 of the walk and the table above it  FORWARD then INVERSE
;   @0x37a        cnt  rounds still to do
;   @0x384:0x453  the schedule buffer{208}  reversed  then shorter each round
;   @0x454:0x463  block/rkreverse208's scratch
;
; THERE IS NO INTERFACE LINE AND THAT IS FORCED  for the reason
; aes/keyexpand128 has none: the S box walk advances three cells a turn  so
; tools/bffoot cannot bound a footprint; This is a PROGRAM;
;
; ASSERT ptr=0
; ASSERT zero 0:1123

; ==== the key goes straight into the window ====
R25
  ,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,
; ASSERT ptr=48

; ==== and the ciphertext into the state ====
R34
  ,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,
; ASSERT ptr=97
L97
; ASSERT ptr=0

; ==== the FORWARD S box  which the schedule reads ====
%%block/aes128table%%
; ASSERT ptr=45
L45
; ASSERT ptr=0

; ==== the whole schedule  in the ordinary order ====
%%block/aeskeyexpand192%%
; ASSERT ptr=0

; ==== the two cells the schedule leaves live ====
; the window still holds the last six words
R25
  [-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>
  [-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]
; ASSERT ptr=48
; and the round constant holds one more than this width asks for
R13
  [-]
; ASSERT ptr=61
L61
; ASSERT ptr=0
; the state holds the ciphertext  which is why the claim stops short of it
; ASSERT zero 25:81

; ==== the forward table is CLEARED  all 768 cells of it ====
; block/invsbox256 is delta coded against noughts and goes in next door;
; written over a live table it would be wrong in 256 places
R117
; cells 117 to 180
  [-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>[-]>
